# Workers Assets' headers on the static files
# (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/):
# `just assets` copies this file into worker-assets/.
# Rules here don't apply to the Worker's own responses, which carry theirs
# from security_headers in crates/server/src/lib.rs: the web app's page
# (index.html, which isn't among these files) included, with its
# Content-Security-Policy.
#
# Every file: no sniffing, the origin only as referrer, and, as the Worker
# sends on whatever isn't a page, no framing. None of these files is a page.
#
# The participant's assets are named by their hash (apps/participant),
# so phones keep them for good; its fallback keeps a fixed name, so phones
# revalidate it, which Assets does by default (max-age=0, must-revalidate,
# with an ETag): this says so. The web app's module and its glue are named by
# their hash too (rafi-web-dxh….js, rafi-web_bg-dxh….wasm); its other files
# (the stylesheet, the fonts, the icons) keep their names and Assets' default.
# A rule takes one splat, so dx's other hashed names (focus-trap-dxh….js,
# 1 KB) keep the default here; the native server keeps them for good.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/participant/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/participant/fallback.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/rafi-web*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
